# life-agent local config — copy to `.env` (gitignored) and set for your machine.
# Primarily NON-SECRET: paths and toggles. On a machine WITH a secret store
# (gnome-keyring), keep API keys there — this project reads them via `secret-tool`.
# Without one (the common case for a new user), `.env` is gitignored, so an
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here is a fine fallback: `secret()` checks the environment
# first, then the keyring (src/life_agent/core/llm.py).
#
# Load into the current shell when working on life-agent:
#     set -a; source .env; set +a
#
# Out-of-tree knowledge base (PII, run outputs). Default if unset: ~/.life-agent/kb
LIFE_AGENT_KB="$HOME/.life-agent/kb"

# Your pkm config.yaml. Default if unset: ~/.config/life-agent/pkm.yaml
# Copy config/pkm.example.yaml there and set its `root_dir` + pandoc version.
PKM_CONFIG="$HOME/.config/life-agent/pkm.yaml"

# API key for answer synthesis (bin/ask-live). Keyring is preferred where present;
# this env fallback is read if set. Building the sample corpus needs no key.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# Optional corpus roots used by build_corpus.sh / needle.sh (else default to $HOME/{...}):
# DOCS_SRC="$HOME/documents"
# NOTES_SRC="$HOME/notes"
# PARSED_SRC="$HOME/parsed"
